{"base_rate":0.4201101928374656,"brier":0.13595000000000002,"bss":0.44195333359292865,"bss_hi":0.521073528950596,"bss_lo":0.3527626543319116,"chart":{"base":[606.7,52.7],"fp":[267.9,312.1],"lead":"62,259.3 272,234.3 482,192 692,113.3","note":{"base":"skill 0.44 — higher than 83% of cities","fp":"low end +7pp, high end +13pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.0 °C — better than 64% of cities","rel":"promised 1% → rained 8%; promised 95% → rained 82%"},"rel":"67,433.1 289.5,332.8 662.9,112.7"},"country":"LU","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.09866391184573003,"ess":305.0277085989247,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Luxembourg</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Luxembourg rain forecast is genuinely useful, though 4 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (99%), believe about\n<b>87%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(1%), there is still roughly a <b>8%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 726 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-04-30. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nLUXEMBOURG AIRPORT, 5.4 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.44, ranked 36 of\n213 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(16&ndash;75) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>1%</td><td class='num'><b>8%</b></td><td class='num'>289</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>19%</td><td class='num'><b>22%</b></td><td class='num'>73</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>54%</td><td class='num'><b>40%</b></td><td class='num'>73</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>83%</td><td class='num'><b>65%</b></td><td class='num'>69</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>99%</td><td class='num'><b>87%</b></td><td class='num'>222</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">4 of 5 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Luxembourg</b> <span class=\"muted\">Luxembourg</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag good\">Genuinely useful</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">4 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.44</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>16&ndash;75\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 213</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>726 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Luxembourg &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Luxembourg\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"60.81730103806228,375.70242214532874 124.29013698630136,282.2739726027397 247.41424657534247,147.64383561643834 350.3834782608696,49.6521739130435 409.68783783783783,18.0 409.68783783783783,24.55855855855856 350.3834782608696,112.95652173913044 247.41424657534247,227.4246575342466 124.29013698630136,342.1095890410959 60.81730103806228,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"229.07988980716252\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"229.07988980716252\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"60.81730103806228,354.29065743944636 124.29013698630136,302.2191780821918 247.41424657534247,237.39726027397262 350.3834782608696,144.6086956521739 409.68783783783783,65.54954954954957\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 1%&amp;#10;It rained 8% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 289 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"60.81730103806228\" cy=\"354.29065743944636\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 19%&amp;#10;It rained 22% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 73 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"124.29013698630136\" cy=\"302.2191780821918\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 54%&amp;#10;It rained 40% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 73 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"247.41424657534247\" cy=\"237.39726027397262\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 83%&amp;#10;It rained 65% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 69 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"350.3834782608696\" cy=\"144.6086956521739\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 99%&amp;#10;It rained 87% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 222 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"409.68783783783783\" cy=\"65.54954954954957\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(42%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Luxembourg the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>winter</b> (0.59) and least in\n<b>spring</b> (0.35).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>187</td><td class='num'>30%</td><td class='num'>0.353</td><td class='num'>9.7%</td></tr><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>184</td><td class='num'>39%</td><td class='num'>0.361</td><td class='num'>11.2%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>50%</td><td class='num'>0.396</td><td class='num'>8.8%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>175</td><td class='num'>49%</td><td class='num'>0.591</td><td class='num'>7.1%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":49.60982,"lon":6.13268,"n":726,"n_cities":213,"name":"Luxembourg","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.08,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.007958477508650518,"n":289,"obs":0.07612456747404844,"sig":true},{"hi":0.35,"lo":0.08,"mean":0.18726027397260273,"n":73,"obs":0.2191780821917808,"sig":false},{"hi":0.71,"lo":0.35,"mean":0.5350684931506849,"n":73,"obs":0.3972602739726027,"sig":true},{"hi":0.94,"lo":0.71,"mean":0.8259420289855074,"n":69,"obs":0.6521739130434783,"sig":true},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.94,"mean":0.9934684684684685,"n":222,"obs":0.8693693693693694,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":5.4,"provisional":false,"rank":36,"rank_hi":75.02499999999998,"rank_lo":16.0,"reliability":0.011440772783368655,"resolution":0.11805047287124085,"skill_pct":null,"slug":"luxembourg","station":"LUXEMBOU